  "term": "psilocin",
  "definition": "Psilocin is a psychoactive tryptamine alkaloid found in some fungi, including Psilocybe. It is the active compound formed from psilocybine in the body and acts in the central nervous system by stimulating serotonin 2A receptors, producing hallucinogenic and anxiolytic effects.",
